.SS "\fBCollider\fP setupCollider ()"

.PP
Create or return the optional whole-body collider\&. Geometry uses particle-local distance units and follows its transform\&. No geometry is inferred from artwork\&. Enable layer collisions and configure shapes for contact detection\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The \fBParticle\fP's \fBCollider\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
ParticleEffects 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBParticleEmitter\fP setupParticleEmitter ()"

.PP
Create or return the owned emitter\&. Repeated calls preserve configuration and identity\&. Its local origin and facing default to zero\&. Reading emitter/getParticleEmitter() never creates it\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The \fBParticle\fP's emitter\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
ParticleEffects 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBPhysicsBody\fP setupPhysicsBody (number mass = \fR1\fP, number momentOfInertia = \fR1\fP)"

.PP
Set up the optional body\&. Applies mass and inertia on every call, defaulting both to 1\&. An existing body preserves identity, mode, velocity, forces and constraints\&. A newly created dynamic body stops programmed movement/spin\&. Immediate owner transform setters teleport the body\&. Read physics for ordinary edits\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImass\fP Finite positive mass; default 1\&. 
.br
\fImomentOfInertia\fP Finite positive inertia; default 1\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The \fBParticle\fP's \fBPhysicsBody\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
ParticleEffects 
.RE
.PP

